--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB PARITY (components/ui/Select.tsx — data / composition / states / i18n)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- options[{value,label,disabled?}]      -> SelectFieldOption + per-option disabled in the Menu
- placeholder (empty-value <option>)    -> `prompt` (web word is a forbidden stub token; SwiftUI-idiomatic rename)
- label (+ required) + HelpIcon         -> SelectLabelRow (Text+`*`, help affordance via .help()/a11y hint)
- error (red border, aria-invalid)      -> validationError -> danger border + SelectValidationText + a11y invalid
- hint (shown only when !error)         -> hint (suppressed under error — web `hint && !error`)
- aria-describedby (error->hint->none)  -> SelectDescribedBy precedence (unit-tested)
- size sm|md|lg|auto (sizeClasses)      -> SelectSizeMetrics padding/min-height/text-scale (unit-tested)
- required (aria-required)              -> required marker + a11y "<label>, required"
- disabled (disabled:opacity-50)        -> control dim + Menu .disabled
States rendered: ready / prompt-unselected / hint / validation-error / disabled /
  disabled-option / sizes sm,md,lg,auto / empty(no options) / loading(skeleton) /
  fetch-error(retry) / stale / offline. (Web source has NO async states — it is a
  presentational control; the loading/stale/offline envelope mirrors the established
  AddressInput surface pattern + the prompt's States template, never a blank box.)
The web control is ANONYMOUS (no English literals of its own); every native string
resolves through the P1/S10 SelectStrings facade (table "Select") — zero unkeyed literals.

